First Author: Sharma
Title: Development and Validation of a Hybrid Machine Learning Model to Predict Lung Transplant Outcomes
Source number: 70

Very short summary: This retrospective US national-registry study included 51,933 adult first-time lung transplant recipients and used a temporal development cohort from 1987–2014 and testing cohort from 2015–2025. The interpretable AutoScore-Survival framework combined random survival forest variable selection with a Cox proportional hazards point score; in the temporal testing cohort, the 1-year time-dependent AUC was 0.61 (95% CI 0.52–0.70), with good reported calibration and positive net benefit on decision-curve analysis.

