	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: AutoScore-Survival is a hybrid framework that used a random survival forest to rank 61 candidate variables and Cox proportional hazards regression to generate an interpretable integer-based score. A parsimony plot in the development validation cohort selected nine predictors. The cohort was temporally split into development and contemporary testing periods; the development cohort was further divided into training and validation sets for model selection and hyperparameter tuning. Interpretability was provided through a nine-variable point score, hazard ratios, risk groups, and a web calculator.

